Mini Marty is a fan-made educational re-implementation inspired by
"Marty the Robot" by Robotical Ltd (Edinburgh, United Kingdom).

"Marty" and "Marty the Robot" are trademarks of Robotical Ltd.
This project is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by
Robotical Ltd. Trademark references in this project's source code,
user interface, and documentation are descriptive and identify the
hardware platform that inspired this educational software. For the
official Marty experience with real hardware, please visit:

  https://codemarty.com    (Robotical's web coding app for Marty)
  https://robotical.io     (Robotical Ltd company site)

The Python API surface exposed by `src/features/python-runtime/`
follows the public method signatures of `martypy`
(https://github.com/robotical/martypy), distributed under the
Apache License 2.0 by Robotical Ltd. Code written for Mini Marty's
virtual robot is therefore portable to the real Marty hardware via
the official `martypy` library.

This project ships no Robotical-owned source code, 3D models,
artwork, audio, logos, or other brand assets. See
`docs/ATTRIBUTION.md` for the full IP audit.
